#!grafli v4
# Who can change a board while it is shown, and how much of the map does it carry? — a matrix
# Worked example of the matrix encoding (skill: references/design.md
# "Matrix on two axes"): every way a board leaves the file, placed on two
# forces. The arrows run from the canvas to what it produces; the one that
# runs to the right is planned.
# source: ..

# ── claim ──
@ note claim 0,-200 "Today a board is either changed by its author or shown as a copy nobody can change" ~xlarge !flat !sans !bold
@ note channel 0,-135 "matrix: x = who can change it while it is shown, y = how much of the map it carries; the empty corner is what the planned live tab fills" ~small !flat !sans

# ── axes ──
@ note o 0,620 "·" !flat
@ note xe 1240,620 "·" !flat
@ note ye 0,-40 "·" !flat
@ arrow o -> xe !thin
@ arrow o -> ye !thin
@ note xl 1060,580 "who can change it →︎" ~small !flat !sans
@ note yl 30,-50 "↑︎ how much of the map it carries" ~small !flat !sans
@ note x0 100,640 "nobody" ~small !flat !sans
@ note x1 500,640 "its author, and their agent" ~small !flat !sans
@ note x2 960,640 "everyone in the call" ~small !flat !sans
@ note y0 -150,490 "one view" ~small !flat !sans
@ note y1 -150,300 "one tour" ~small !flat !sans
@ note y2 -150,110 "every level and tour" ~small !flat !sans

# ── items ──
@ box html "HTML page" 60,80 240x80
@ box slides "PDF / PPTX deck" 60,270 240x80
@ box render "PNG / SVG render" 60,460 240x80
@ box canvas "desktop canvas" 480,80 240x80 %primary !ink !sans
@ box tab "live tab, planned" 920,80 240x80 %accent !ink !dashed !bold

# ── produces ──
@ arrow canvas -> html "export-html: every board"
@ arrow canvas -> slides "export: 1 tour"
@ arrow canvas -> render "render: 1 view"
@ arrow canvas -> tab "serve: #262" !dashed
